Z||000003||Eric||04-07-2000||08:12 PM||||Last time I was there, at Indy, it rained cats and dogs.  Overall it was a wet pile of carbon fiber and motor oil.  Too bad too, the grid was filled up with cart racers and it would have been a treat to see them all trying to qualify.  Today's 500 doesn't intrigue me too much.  To tell you the truth, I wish all the problems between CART and Indy cars were rectified so they could get on with open wheel racing.  I used to side with CART, letting the turbo cars back to Indy, but with the recent death of a great racer, Greg Moore, I have to say the best thing for the future of American open wheel racing is the car found in the IRL.  I hope everything pans out in the future so we all can continue watching the best race car drivers America has to offer in the greatest race of all time, the Indy 500.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87ECO5||05-15-2000||09:34 AM||||OK - here's what I've got ...<P>Looks like we've got myself, ChadMan and BOILERMAKER meeting at the track between 10:30 and 10:45 at gate E/B:<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/indytrack.jpg"> <P>Right now, The Weather Channel is calling for partly cloudy skies.<P>Anyone else interested?  Oh ya, I think a few of us will be at the Dayton, Ohio Cracker Barrel around 8:30 for some breakfast before heading over to Indy.  And, we're planning to do something afterwards too.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Monkeyman||05-15-2000||09:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87ECO5:<BR><B>Anyone going next month?...</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Umm...I'm fairly certain it's this month <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.  I wish I could make it, but I'll have to work (what a surprise).  The Grape Ape has some brake problems so I'd be afraid to drive that far.  As soon as I can come up with $100 I'll probably do the Beretta upgrade to the back and see what happens.  (Brake light on and LOTS of pedal travel)  Can we do something around the middle of next month???  I miss you guys. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Hopefully the Grape Ape will be roadworthy by then and I'll get a day or two off.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||87ECO5||05-15-2000||10:57 AM||||Monkeyman - when I posted the original note (last month), this month would have been next month, silly!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Middle of next month (would that be this month or June!?    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">   ) ... fiero56, WT3 and I are driving to Farmington Hills, MI for the Fiero show on the 16th.  Then there's the Mid-Ohio show on the 25th.<P>We miss you too, pal!||||reg||1
